WEBVTT

00:03:25.904 --> 00:03:30.264
And by "political" I mean poetry 
is political in at least three ways:

00:03:30.264 --> 00:03:34.261
One: what stories we tell,
when we're telling them,

00:03:34.261 --> 00:03:36.571
how we're telling them,
if we're telling them,

00:03:36.571 --> 00:03:39.392
why we're telling them,
says so much about

00:03:39.392 --> 00:03:41.242
the political 
beliefs we have,


00:03:41.242 --> 00:03:43.722
about what types 
of stories matter.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:46.292
Secondly, who gets to 
have their stories told,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.002
I'm talking, who is legally 
allowed to read,

00:03:49.002 --> 00:03:51.492
who has the resources 
to be able to write,

00:03:51.492 --> 00:03:53.342
who are we reading 
in our classrooms,

00:03:53.342 --> 00:03:56.982
says a lot about the political 
and educational systems,

00:03:56.982 --> 00:04:00.132
that all these stories and 
storytellers exist in.